<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<vmAdvParameters>
<!--
  Virtual machine advanced parameters to collect (VCF Content Factory
  vCommunity).

  Name the advanced configuration parameters (the keys that appear in a
  virtual machine's .vmx file, vSphere's "extra configuration") whose value
  you want on each virtual machine. A virtual machine that does not carry the
  parameter publishes nothing for it. Names are case sensitive.

  Format
    - Separate entries with commas. A line break does NOT separate entries.
    - An XML comment, like this one, is ignored. To switch an entry on, move
      it out of the comment, and keep the comma after it.
    - Do not write two hyphens in a row inside a comment.

  Do not edit this shipped file: every upgrade of the pack replaces it and
  your edits are lost (measured on VCF Operations 9.0.2 and 9.1.1, even without force
  content update). Back the files up before an upgrade. Make a copy under another name in the VCF Operations configuration-file store, and
  enter that name (no .xml) in the account's VM Advanced Parameters Config
  File field.
  As shipped, every entry is commented out, so nothing is collected.

  Examples, one per line:
    disk.EnableUUID,
    isolation.tools.copy.disable,
    isolation.tools.paste.disable,
    isolation.tools.dnd.disable,
    tools.guestlib.enableHostInfo,
-->
</vmAdvParameters>
